          "title": "Java I/O Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bytes vs Characters",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Byte streams",
                "Character streams"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Classes",
                  "`InputStream` / `OutputStream`",
                  "`Reader` / `Writer`"
                ],
                [
                  "Unit",
                  "raw ==8-bit== bytes",
                  "==16-bit== chars"
                ],
                [
                  "Charset",
                  "none",
                  "decodes / encodes via a charset"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "images, PDFs, zips, any binary",
                  "text"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bridge classes== `InputStreamReader` / `OutputStreamWriter` turn a byte stream into a character stream",
                "Always give the bridge an **explicit** `Charset`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Decorator Layers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Decorator pattern: each wrapper adds ==one job== around the stream inside it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "FileInputStream",
                    "sub": "raw bytes",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "InputStreamReader",
                    "sub": "decode with UTF_8",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "BufferedReader",
                    "sub": "chunks and lines",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "var br = new BufferedReader(",
                "    new InputStreamReader(",
                "        new FileInputStream(f), UTF_8));"
              ],
              "note": "bytes, then decode, then buffer"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Reader on binary data",
              "text": "A `Reader` on an image or zip **corrupts** it: decoding ==replaces invalid bytes==. Use `InputStream` for binary."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "try-with-resources and BufferedReader",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "try-with-resources and BufferedReader",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. try-with-resources",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`try (var r = new BufferedReader(...)) { }` closes any ==AutoCloseable==",
                "Closes even when an {red:exception} is thrown",
                "Closing the outer wrapper closes the inner stream",
                "Close order is ==reverse== of declaration",
                "A failing `close()` is {purple:suppressed}: read it with `getSuppressed()`",
                "The primary exception is not lost"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Open in",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Open br",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Body",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Close br",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Close in",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading lines",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`readLine()` returns ==null== at end of file",
                "It strips the line terminator",
                "Reads in chunks (default ==8192== chars): fewer system calls"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "try (var br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(f))) {",
                "    String line;",
                "    while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {",
                "        use(line);",
                "    }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Writing and review",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`BufferedWriter` holds text until `flush()`",
                "`newLine()` ends a line",
                "Flush happens on `close()`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Skipping `close()` and `flush()` loses ==buffered text==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Close order?** Reverse of declaration.",
                "**close() throws too?** Suppressed, not lost.",
                "**readLine() at EOF?** Returns null."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Path and Files Essentials",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Path and Files Essentials",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Path: a location object",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Path== is an **immutable** location: `Path.of(\"a\",\"b.txt\")` or `Paths.get(...)`",
                "It may ==not exist== on disk; creating one touches nothing",
                "Operations are **pure string logic**, no disk access"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`resolve(other)`",
                  "**appends** other to this path"
                ],
                [
                  "`relativize(other)`",
                  "computes the **relative** path between two"
                ],
                [
                  "`normalize()`",
                  "removes `.` and `..`"
                ],
                [
                  "`toAbsolutePath()`",
                  "anchors to the **cwd**"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Files: everyday actions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Checks: `exists`, `notExists`, `isDirectory`, `size`",
                "Actions: `delete`, `deleteIfExists`, `createDirectories`",
                "`copy` and `move` between paths"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Files.copy(src, dst,",
                "    StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);",
                "Files.move(src, dst,",
                "    StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE);"
              ],
              "note": "without REPLACE_EXISTING: FileAlreadyExistsException"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`copy`/`move` throw ==FileAlreadyExistsException== if target exists",
                "==REPLACE_EXISTING== overwrites the target",
                "==ATOMIC_MOVE== requests an atomic rename"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Legacy java.io.File",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`File` reports failure with a **boolean**, not an exception",
                "Prefer `Path` and `Files`",
                "Convert: `file.toPath()` and `path.toFile()`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Does `Path.of(\"x\")` create a file? **No**. What does `normalize()` do? Removes `.`/`..`. Why prefer `Files` over `File`? **Exceptions** explain failures."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
